// A `@debug` GENERIC instantiated with an undebug-able argument. The skeleton is
// not refused - its payload is a type variable, which is debug-able in no
// direction - so the refusal lands on the INSTANCE and borrows the skeleton's
// position, naming the instance the way the reader would write it.
//
// The reference guards this with "declares no type parameters". The port's index
// does not carry those on a skeleton entry, so the guard here asks the property
// that one stands for: are the field types real yet.
struct Plain { v: int }
@debug enum G<T> { A(T) | B }
fn main() { let g: G<Plain> = G::A(Plain { v: 1 }); println(g); }
